                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "70925559",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561198062124970",
                            "num_reviews": 1,
                            "playtime_forever": 1330,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 1299,
                            "last_played": 1601819143
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I'm usually not a huge fan of puzzle games, which is why I was surprised by how much fun I had with Puzzle Party. The difficulty varies, some levels were easy, some it took me a lot of trial and error to figure out, but even I with my pea brain eventually managed to beat all 92 of them one way or another.\nThe game has a story, which is probably its weakest point. Still, while it never really captivated me all that much, I also never found it distracting either.\nTo me, Puzzle Party’s strongest point is the atmosphere. I never felt frustrated, even when I messed up a level for the tenth time. Something about the space background, the deep rumble of the ambient noise, and the simple graphics just has a calming effect on me (also the sound effects, which all have a super satisfying crunchiness to them).\nTo sum it up: Puzzle Party is a nice little game with some creative and challenging puzzles, an okay plot, and a really cosy atmosphere. I’d say for the cheap price, you can’t go wrong, and it’s a great game to play on your break!",
